+### Deviation from T038/T045: two pre-existing assertions had to be relaxed
+
+T038 and T045 require the diff to touch no pre-existing test module. **That gate could not be
+met**, because two 001 tests pinned the JSON read body to *exactly* four keys:
+
+- `tests/test_read.py::test_FR_009_json_read_returns_the_four_fields`
+- `tests/test_create.py::test_FR_007_unknown_fields_are_ignored_not_rejected`
+
+FR-054 requires `burn_after_reading` and `protected` to be *added* to that body, so those two
+assertions and FR-054 cannot both hold — no implementation of FR-054 can keep them green.
+
+Resolved in favour of FR-054, on the grounds that the assertions were stricter than the
+requirement they covered: 001's FR-009 requires a body **"containing** `id`, `content`,
+`created_at`, and `expires_at`", not exactly those. Both were changed from `sorted(body) == [...]`
+to `set(body) >= {...}`, which is what FR-009 actually specifies; every other assertion in both
+tests is untouched, and the exact six-field shape is now pinned by
+`test_compat.py::test_FR_054_FR_055_json_read_body_is_exactly_six_fields`. Net change to
+pre-existing tests: `test_create.py` +3/-1, `test_read.py` +8/-2 (mostly explanatory docstring);
+the other five 001 modules are byte-for-byte unchanged. Recorded in `tests/README.md` under
+"Note on SC-017 and the two relaxed 001 assertions".
+
+**SC-017's literal wording ("the existing test suite passes unmodified") is therefore not
+satisfiable as written** and should be amended to exempt FR-054's two added fields.
+
+### Two transport constraints found while testing FR-043
+
+Neither is an implementation defect; both are properties of carrying a password in an HTTP
+header, and both are now documented by tests rather than worked around:
+
+1. **Leading whitespace cannot be carried.** RFC 7230 defines a field value as `OWS field-value
+   OWS`, so the parser strips whitespace before the value. Supplying `" pw"` for a paste whose
+   password is `"pw"` therefore *succeeds*, and a paste created with a leading-whitespace password
+   cannot be read at all (it stays deletable by its token). Trailing whitespace is preserved and
+   is matched exactly. Test: `test_FR_043_leading_whitespace_cannot_be_carried_in_a_header`.
+2. **Characters outside latin-1 cannot be carried.** HTTP header values are US-ASCII plus
+   `obs-text`, and `http.client` enforces latin-1, so a CJK or emoji password is accepted at
+   creation (FR-036 permits it) and handled correctly by storage, but no conforming client can
+   present it. Test: `test_FR_043_a_password_outside_latin_1_cannot_be_carried_in_a_header`.
+
+Compensating for either in the comparison would break FR-043's "compared exactly", so both are
+recorded as constraints. A future spec revision may wish to narrow FR-036's accepted character
+set to what the header can actually carry.
+
+### Test-name convention
+
+Test names use the **uppercase** `FR_0nn` form (`test_FR_047_...`), matching the 001 suite and the
+`pytest -k FR_013` selection documented in `tests/README.md`. The quickstart's coverage snippet
+greps lowercase `fr_0`; use `grep -ci fr_0` (case-insensitive). All of FR-033…FR-060 appear in at
+least one collected test name (T042, SC-016); SC-016 itself is the traceability table, as 001
+treats SC-002.
