+## Note on SC-017 and the two relaxed 001 assertions
+
+SC-017 asks for the 001 suite to pass *unmodified*. Two 001 tests had pinned the JSON read body
+to **exactly** four keys:
+
+- `test_read.py::test_FR_009_json_read_returns_the_four_fields`
+- `test_create.py::test_FR_007_unknown_fields_are_ignored_not_rejected`
+
+Feature 002's **FR-054** requires `burn_after_reading` and `protected` to be added to that body,
+so those two assertions and FR-054 cannot both hold. 001's **FR-009** itself only requires a body
+*"containing* `id`, `content`, `created_at`, and `expires_at`" — the `== [four keys]` assertions
+were stricter than the requirement they covered. Both were therefore relaxed to containment
+(`set(body) >= {...}`), which is exactly what FR-009 specifies; every other assertion in both
+tests is untouched. The exact six-field shape is now pinned by
+`test_compat.py::test_FR_054_FR_055_json_read_body_is_exactly_six_fields`.
